<title>HUNGARY: Hungary 3-yr bond yield rises 61 bps to 17.75 pct.</title>
<headline>Hungary 3-yr bond yield rises 61 bps to 17.75 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average annual yield on the latest issue of Hungary's three-year government bonds was set by auction at 17.75 percent, up from 17.14 percent fixed at an auction four weeks ago, the Government Debt Management Agency (AKK) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>BONDS OF THE 2000/F SERIES</p>
<p>    First day of interest    July 7, 1997</p>
<p>    Date of maturity	   Aug 24, 2000</p>
<p>    Bonds on offer	    17,500 million forints Maximum</p>
<p>    Total bids received     40,616.18 million forints</p>
<p>    Total allocated	   14,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total issued		18,200 million forints</p>
<p>    Average annual yield	  17.75 pct</p>
<p>    Average price		   97.46 pct</p>
<p>NOTE: The bond bears a fixed interest rate of 16.00 percent, payable semi-anually starting from February 24, 1998.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
